IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-arbitration`
IMPORT `caa-qa`

-- Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (caa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role
-- and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading a BOOLEAN, NUMBER or DATE input that is ASSUMEd stops the
-- evaluation with an error. Each question with a situation input is asked, for its role, with each value under which
-- the situation does not hold and every later input ASSUMEd (for the award: no award yet; for enforcing, also an award
-- wholly against me; for resisting, also an award wholly in my favour). Those two groups are generated from the
-- parameter lists (scratchpad qa_params.py) and come last. The hand-worked cases come first: each answer is worked by
-- hand from the deposited text, and for the party (the baseline's seat) each question is also asserted equal to the
-- baseline export's answer on the same facts. Life facts: d038 and d051, with the baseline's ASSUMPTIONS (a signed
-- written contract between two Perth businesses, seated in Perth; no arbitration on foot for d051); the 2030-2031 dates
-- are hypothetical.
--
-- `The award and me` is read only through the three award helpers, which list every value with no OTHERWISE, so an
-- ASSUMEd award value fails if read.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked The award and me` IS A `The award and me`

`as a party` MEANS `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration`
`as the arbitrator` MEANS `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one`

`an award in my favour` MEANS `an award has been made, in my favour`
`an award against me` MEANS `an award has been made, against me`
`an award partly each way` MEANS `an award has been made, partly in my favour and partly against me`

`d038, a signed contract with an arbitration clause, as a record` MEANS `My arbitration agreement` WITH
    `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` IS TRUE
    `its content is recorded in some form` IS TRUE
    `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS FALSE
    `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS FALSE
    `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause it makes part of the contract` IS FALSE
    `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` IS TRUE
    `the relationship is commercial` IS TRUE
    `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` IS FALSE
    `the place of arbitration is in Western Australia` IS TRUE

`three arbitrators, the other side silent for 31 days, as a record` MEANS `My appointment facts` WITH
    `we agreed an appointment procedure` IS FALSE
    `under it a party failed to act, agreement failed, or an institution failed to act` IS FALSE
    `the procedure provides other means of securing the appointment` IS FALSE
    `the number of arbitrators` IS 3
    `the number of parties` IS 2
    `we agree on the sole arbitrator` IS FALSE
    `days since the other party received my request to appoint, still not appointing` IS 31
    `days since the two party arbitrators were appointed, still no third` IS 0

`the oral hearing I asked for refused, as a record` MEANS `How I was heard` WITH
    `I was treated equally with the other party` IS TRUE
    `I had a reasonable opportunity to present my case` IS TRUE
    `I asked for an oral hearing` IS TRUE
    `we agreed that no hearings would be held` IS FALSE
    `an oral hearing was held` IS FALSE
    `I had sufficient advance notice of every hearing and inspection` IS TRUE
    `everything the other party gave the tribunal was communicated to me` IS TRUE
    `every expert report or document the tribunal may rely on was communicated to me` IS TRUE

`no proper notice, applying on 15 August 2030, as a record` MEANS `My setting-aside application` WITH
    `I prove a party lacked capacity or the agreement is invalid` IS FALSE
    `I prove I had no proper notice or could not present my case` IS TRUE
    `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration` IS FALSE
    `the part beyond the submission can be separated` IS FALSE
    `I prove the tribunal or procedure departed from our agreement or the Act` IS FALSE
    `the Court finds the dispute not capable of settlement by arbitration` IS FALSE
    `the Court finds the award against the public policy of Western Australia` IS FALSE
    `the date I received the award` IS (Date 1 6 2030)
    `a section 33 request was made` IS FALSE
    `the date the tribunal disposed of it` IS (Date 1 6 2030)
    `the date I apply` IS (Date 15 8 2030)

`a question of law, agreed, obviously wrong, as a record` MEANS `My appeal` WITH
    `it is a question of law arising out of the award` IS TRUE
    `the parties agreed to an appeal before the appeal period ended` IS TRUE
    `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` IS TRUE
    `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it` IS TRUE
    `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong` IS TRUE
    `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` IS FALSE
    `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` IS TRUE
    `the date I received the award` IS (Date 1 6 2030)
    `a section 33 request was made` IS FALSE
    `the date the tribunal disposed of it` IS (Date 1 6 2030)
    `the date I appeal` IS (Date 15 8 2030)

